ATTRIBUTION
================================================================================

Authored and edited by Nathan Woodman.

Substantial architectural and editorial input was provided by:

- Ether Data Research — particularly Laurent Madeleni (four-phase architecture,
  context-envelope framing, "open the envelope, keep the models proprietary"
  governance posture) and Yuri Khrakovsky (standards-alignment perspective,
  serving-API requirements).
- Damian Naglak, Bedrock Platform (segments-vs-embeddings practitioner framing).
- The IAB Tech Lab AAMP initiative — ARTF, Agentic Audiences (formerly the
  LiveRamp User Context Protocol), buyer/seller agent SDKs.

Conceptual debt is acknowledged to the multi-tower and sequence-learning
recommendation architectures pioneered at YouTube (Covington et al. 2016),
Meta (DLRM, HSTU, MTIA), TikTok (Monolith), and Pinterest (PinSage), as well
as to the H3 hexagonal grid system developed at Uber.

